# NOTICE

`dsh-llm-fusion` packages two independently maintained DSH plugins. Both are
MIT-licensed; their licenses are reproduced verbatim in this repository, and
each engine's source is vendored under `src/engines/<name>` with the upstream
version that was vendored.

## dsh-opencode-go

- Upstream: https://github.com/Duskriver/dsh-opencode-go
- Vendored version: 0.2.1
- Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek
- Copyright (c) 2026 dsh-opencode-go contributors
- License: MIT (see `LICENSE-opencode-go`)

### Local changes against upstream 0.2.1

1. `src/engines/opencode-go/adapter.ts` — the fallback wire identity for calls
   that arrive without a Session id (`title generation`, probes, compaction) is
   now stable per adapter instance instead of a fresh UUID per call, and every
   request carries `x-deepseek-harness-session-id` beside `x-opencode-session`.
   Rationale: the gateway then accounts non-conversational traffic under one
   session instead of creating a session (and a prompt-cache key) per call, and
   the vendor's native header is present on model paths where the OpenCode
   header is not yet threaded. This is a deliberate behaviour change; the two
   upstream tests that asserted the old contract were updated with it.

2. Interaction with `dsh-llm-fusion`: none beyond the package boundary. The
   engine keeps its own loader entry id, settings namespace and routes.

## dsh-protocom-api

- Upstream: https://github.com/AIMFllyYS/dsh-protocom-api
- Vendored version: 1.4.0
- Copyright (c) 2026 AIMFllyYS
- License: MIT (see `LICENSE-protocom`)

### Local changes against upstream 1.4.0

1. `src/engines/protocom/adapter.ts` — the value sent in the session-scoping
   header is reduced to a legal, bounded wire value: visible ASCII ids pass
   through unchanged, anything else (non-ASCII, control characters, an id
   already inside the reserved mapped namespace, or one longer than 64
   characters) is hashed with SHA-256 over UTF-16LE and base64url-encoded.
   Upstream sent `String(sessionId)` verbatim, which can put non-ASCII text or
   an over-long value into an HTTP header.

2. `src/engines/protocom/client/index.ts` and `client/locale.ts` — the OpenCode
   Go subscription tab registers under the slot id `opencode-go-sub` instead of
   `OPENCODE_GO.ns` (`opencode-go`), and its labels read "OpenCode Go
   (subscription)". Upstream could use `opencode-go` because it shipped alone;
   in this bundle the OpenCode Go engine already registers that
   `settings.section` id, and the slot registry refuses two entries with one id
   at one priority, so the duplicate registration aborted the rest of the
   Protocom tab set. Only the UI slot key and its copy changed: Protocom reads
   and writes its settings through Loader entry `protocom-api` plus section
   key, never through the slot id, so no stored value moves.

3. Interaction with `dsh-llm-fusion`: none beyond the package boundary.

## Why a packaging merge and not a source rewrite

The two engines implement their wire layers differently: `dsh-opencode-go`
delegates to the `pi-ai` SDK and carries a bespoke conversion/transport layer,
while `dsh-protocom-api` implements the chat-completions, Responses and
Anthropic Messages wires itself and drives them through a generic
`ProviderFamily` abstraction. Folding one into the other would mean rewriting
roughly 12k lines of source and re-validating roughly 9k lines of tests for
each side, and then tracking two upstreams in the merged tree. `v0.1` therefore
keeps both engines intact, byte-identical apart from the two changes above, and
merges at the packaging, routing, settings and client boundaries — see
`README.md`.
